.TH HSTEX-PDFLATEX 1
.SH NAME
hstex-pdflatex \- run a LaTeX document with the HSTeX engine
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hstex-pdflatex
.RI [ options ] " document.tex"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hstex-pdflatex
is the compatibility front end for HSTeX. It uses the installed TeX Live or
MacTeX tree for LaTeX package and font inputs, builds an HSTeX-native format,
and runs the document from that format. It does not read pdfTeX format dumps.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI -output-directory= dir
Write output files below
.IR dir .
The long form is also accepted.
.TP
.BI -jobname= name
Use
.I name
for output file names and for
.BR \e jobname .
The long form is also accepted.
.TP
.B -interaction=errorstopmode
Select the current HSTeX interaction mode.
.TP
.BR -halt-on-error , " " -file-line-error , " " -no-shell-escape
Supported compatibility options.
.TP
.B -output-format=pdf
Select PDF output.
.TP
.BI --format-cache= dir
Store native LaTeX formats below
.IR dir .
.TP
.B --rebuild-format
Rebuild the native LaTeX format even when a matching cache entry exists.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B HSTEX_CACHE_DIR
The default root of the native format cache.
.TP
.B HSTEX_ENGINE
The HSTeX executable to invoke. This is useful for testing an unpacked build.
.SH EXIT STATUS
The command exits with 2 for an unsupported option or invalid invocation. An
engine or input failure has a nonzero engine status.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/hstex
Default native format cache when
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
is set.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/hstex
Default native format cache otherwise.
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR hstex (1),
.IR kpsewhich (1)
